7] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442311 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186442313 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186442309 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442321 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d0e871fb-e944-567c-b4fe-9835a0a9327f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186442319 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1069 "q-210785" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1071 "Given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{2}{9}x+\\frac{8}{9},\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 0,\\, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nits cumulative distribution function is \n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0,\\, & x<1 \\\\ h(x),\\, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1,\\, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $h(x)=${{field-1}}." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "990f1bb6-e595-59df-8c02-d323344bc3ca" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442324 #edb/ref 1074 "Since our random variable $X$ has a probability distribution function $f(x)$ that is strictly positive only for $1\\le x\\le 4,$ the cumulative distribution function takes the following form:\n\n$$\nF(x)=P(X\\le x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ {\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t, & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the given probability density function, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{x}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t & ={\\int }_{1}^{x}(-\\frac{2}{9}t+\\frac{8}{9})\\,\\text{d}t \\\\ \\text{ } & ={(-\\frac{1}{9}{t}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}t)|}_{1}^{x} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{8}{9}x-\\frac{7}{9} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}({x}^{2}-8x+7) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the cumulative distribution function is given by\n\n$$\nF(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}0, & x<1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{9}(x-1)(x-7), & 1\\le x\\le 4 \\\\ 1, & x>4.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442326 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442330 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442326 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "24fe79a9-1c18-5367-b5d5-50f26230d23d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442326 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442322 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442327 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442326 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442327 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "443e51e5-e403-51ae-bbff-e563149f49e5" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442327 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442325 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442328 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "7a43148a-546c-5e25-817d-f6a542bfe3c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442328 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442324 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442329 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442327 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442329 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "989b9a58-4363-5017-8054-1b3f417bd0d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442329 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186134539 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442330 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186442328 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442330 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "cdf24c85-fec2-557e-990a-b96c38922ff0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186442330 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186442323 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186500401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186500402 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186500408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186500442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186500450 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045464 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186499644 #edb/ref 1045 "Cumulati